  "releaseNotes": "v4.0.0 - Aligned to Feedemy.KeyManagement 4.0.0\n\n- The rules that match API names are retargeted to the 4.0 surface\n  (KM0001, KM0002, KM0101, KM0103, KM0203, KM0501, KM0502, KM0504, KM1001,\n  KM1201, KM1402); the configuration rules name the With* builder methods.\n- KM0103 reports key material (a GetMaterialAsync result or its Content,\n  an ExportPrivateKeyAsync result or its Pkcs8, an RSA or ECDsa\n  Export*PrivateKey* / ToXmlString(true) result) that reaches a string\n  interpolation or a log call; a lookup's Status, Version or KeyState is\n  not reported.\n- New: KM0705 (warning) flags a private key leaving the library:\n  IAsymmetricKeyOperations.ExportPrivateKeyAsync, and\n  KeyMaterialSerializer.Deserialize of a GetMaterialAsync result.\n- Removed: KM0102 (it could not fire), KM0401 (the obsolete Use* methods\n  it flagged are gone) and KM0701-KM0704 (none could fire on the 4.0\n  surface).\n- 47 rules are declared; 21 of them are raised (docs/ANALYZER_RULES.md).",
